    "story": "Secrets, distance, and the danger. Eyes lock. More than stone and sage divide them. Separated by more than stone and sage, two worlds collide. Judgment from above, questions from below.\nThe hush of looming fate hangs heavy in the air.",
    "notes": "“On the Divide” is a study in tension and ambiguity—classic themes in Western art. The composition uses elevation and distance not only to separate the riders, but to hint at cultural and personal divides that run deeper than the land itself. Painterly textures and subdued color palette draw the viewer’s eye from the stone outcrop to the horizon, rewarding slow looking with subtle detail. For collectors, this piece offers both visual drama and a story that never quite resolves—an open question, held in the hush of looming fate.",
